:["math:functional-equations","math:function-composition-iteration","cnm_162","cnm_h098","cnm_h102","cnm_h101","cnm_h097","cnm_156"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:768f91337a9287bf06fa79a7"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E, 220/3^10","reason":"If k selections have modulus √2, then |P|=2^(3k/2-12), so |P|=1 requires k=8. This has probability C(12,8)(1/3)^8(2/3)^4. Conditional on this event, the four smaller factors make the product's argument uniform among the four multiples of π/2. Thus P(P=-1)=C(12,8)(1/3)^8(2/3)^4/4=220/3^10.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h098"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"2017_AMC_12A_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"moduli-and-forced-factor","label":"Magnitudes and a forced final factor","methodDirectNodeIds":{"moduli-and-forced-factor":["cnm_h098","cnm_h102","cnm_h104","cnm_h137","cnm_h239"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h098","cnm_h102","cnm_h104","cnm_h137","cnm_h239"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:768f91337a9287bf06fa79a7"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A, 20","reason":"The roots are ±(sqrt(10) + i*sqrt(6)) and ±(sqrt(3) + i). The parallelogram has area 2*|sqrt(10) - sqrt(18)| = 6*sqrt(2) - 2*sqrt(10). Thus p + q + r + s = 6 + 2 + 2 + 10 = 20.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h098"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"2018_AMC_12A_Q22","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"cartesian-roots-shoelace","label":"Complex roots and coordinate area","methodDirectNodeIds":{"cartesian-roots-shoelace":["cnm_h099","cnm_h102","cnm_h098","math:shoelace-formula","cnm_224","cnm_183"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h099","cnm_h102","cnm_h098","math:shoelace-formula","cnm_224","cnm_183"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:768f91337a9287bf06fa79a7","alignment:78c98be15b7f15670862fca0"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A (13)","reason":"The segment has length sqrt(3^2+4^2)=5. Its radius-1 neighborhood has area 5·2+π·1^2=10+π, approximately 13.142, whose nearest integer is 13.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h098","cnm_h101"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"2022_AMC_12A_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"segment-neighborhood-area","label":"Thicken the segment","methodDirectNodeIds":{"segment-neighborhood-area":["cnm_h098","cnm_h101","cnm_h173","cnm_p150","cnm_p089","cnm_p192"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h098","cnm_h101","cnm_h173","cnm_p150","cnm_p089","cnm_p192"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:768f91337a9287bf06fa79a7"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A: 6","reason":"Set w = z+2i. The polynomial becomes w^3+w+10 = (w+2)(w^2-2w+5), with roots -2 and 1+/-2i. Thus the original roots are -2-2i, 1, and 1-4i. The last two form a vertical base of length 4, and the first has horizontal distance 3 from that base. The area is 4*3/2 = 6.","status":"matches"},"assessed":true,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h098"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"2025_AMC_12A_Q17","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h100"],"id":"center-shift-and-factor","label":"Translate the variable and factor","methodDirectNodeIds":{"center-shift-and-factor":["math:polynomial-remainder-factor","math:complex-quadratic-solutions","cnm_h098","cnm_p148"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h100","math:polynomial-remainder-factor","math:complex-quadratic-solutions","cnm_h098","cnm_p148"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:768f91337a9287bf06fa79a7"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: point C","reason":"F lies in the first quadrant outside the unit circle. If F=x+iy, then 1/F=(x-iy)/(x²+y²), which lies in the fourth quadrant and has modulus less than 1. Point C is the only displayed point satisfying both conditions.","status":"matches"},"assesse